  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Assistance and Protection Support to Rohingya in Indonesia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this project, IOM is contributing to joint efforts with the Government of Indonesia, international and local partners, and civil society, to provide lifesaving and transitional assistance to Rohingya Refugees in Indonesia, host communities, and new refugees forecasted to arrive during the duration of project implementation. Assistance is being channeled through interventions in various priority areas such as the strengthening of coordination with national and sub-national governments, the provision of sustainable and decent accommodation, primary health services and nutrition supply, mental health and psychosocial support and education, protection, including the prevention of sexual exploitation and abuse and trafficking in person, and any other immediate support as identified.</narrative>
  </description>
